This software and its source code are proprietary and confidential. They are not
open source. No licence is granted except as set out below or in a separate
written agreement signed by Rittman Analytics.

1. Grant

Rittman Analytics grants a named licensee a non-exclusive, non-transferable,
revocable licence to run this software for the sole purpose of producing reports
and suggestions about repositories the licensee owns or is authorised to assess.

2. Restrictions

The licensee may not:

  a. copy, publish, distribute, sublicense, sell or lease the software or its
     source code;
  b. modify the software or create derivative works from it;
  c. remove or obscure the attribution required by clause 4;
  d. use the software to provide an assessment service to a third party without
     a separate written agreement.

3. What the software does not do

By design, and as a term of this licence, the software:

  a. never modifies the licensee's code;
  b. never creates commits, branches or pull requests;
  c. never writes to any data warehouse, and requires only read access to
     warehouse metadata where warehouse access is granted at all;
  d. reads metadata and aggregate counts only, and does not read, store or
     publish row-level data.

4. Attribution

Every report, site and comment the software publishes carries a Rittman
Analytics attribution footer. That footer must remain intact.

5. Suggestions are suggestions

Output is advisory. Every finding names the rule and the evidence behind it. The
licensee remains responsible for decisions taken about its own repositories and
data.

6. No warranty

The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
implied, including the warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular
purpose and non-infringement. To the maximum extent permitted by law, Rittman
Analytics is not liable for any claim, damage or other liability arising from
the software or its use.

7. Termination

This licence ends automatically if the licensee breaches any term. On
termination the licensee must stop using the software and destroy all copies.

